PP-OCRv6 recognition model
--------------------------

PP-OCRv6_rec_pruned.onnx is built into vbt-scoreboard and published at
https://files.akhilnarang.dev/cdn/valorant/ocr/v1/. It is derived from PP-OCRv6_rec_tiny.onnx by
PaddleOCR (https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR), as converted to ONNX by
RapidOCR (https://github.com/RapidAI/RapidOCR), v3.9.2, sha256
e16e242de5937ad92609223f19bc2aff3727ee40b095f996907c24749bad251b.
This project does not redistribute the unmodified model.

  PaddleOCR: Copyright (c) 2016 PaddlePaddle Authors. All Rights Reserved.
  RapidOCR: Copyright (c) 2021 RapidOCR Authors. All rights reserved.
            Copyright (c) 2021 RapidAI. All rights reserved.

The model is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; a copy is in
LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt. The published model file is modified (pruned, as
described below). Its Apache-2.0 licence text and this notice are published
next to it at
https://files.akhilnarang.dev/cdn/valorant/ocr/v1/LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt and
https://files.akhilnarang.dev/cdn/valorant/ocr/v1/NOTICE.txt.

Modification: scoreboard/tools/prune_head.py slices the model's classification
head to the 128 classes the scoreboard reads (blank, printable ASCII, the
Latin-1 letters, space) and trims the character list to match. Nothing else
in the model is changed.

imaging resize
--------------

vision/src/resample.rs is a Rust port of Resize from imaging v1.6.2
(https://github.com/disintegration/imaging), Copyright (c) 2012 Grigory
Dryapak, MIT licensed; the licence text is in LICENSES/imaging-MIT.txt. The
port keeps imaging's arithmetic so its output matches pixel for pixel, which
the glyph templates and the digit classifier were built on.

